1
00:00:08,975 --> 00:00:09,976
No good.

2
00:00:10,610 --> 00:00:13,947
I think I can use the Superior
Mesenteric Artery First Approach.

3
00:00:14,514 --> 00:00:15,515
No,

4
00:00:15,582 --> 00:00:17,384
there should still be time.

5
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:19,786
Dr. Ebina looks so serious.

6
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:21,654
It must be a difficult procedure.

7
00:00:21,721 --> 00:00:22,655
No.

8
00:00:22,722 --> 00:00:24,324
He's getting tickets for a musical.

9
00:00:25,158 --> 00:00:27,560
He's battling for front-row seats
on opening night.

10
00:00:29,529 --> 00:00:30,397
SITE UNAVAILABLE: TOO MANY CONNECTIONS

11
00:00:30,463 --> 00:00:31,898
Damn it!

12
00:00:32,565 --> 00:00:33,533
Please!

13
00:00:35,635 --> 00:00:37,270
With a Director of Surgery like him,

14
00:00:37,337 --> 00:00:39,406
no wonder they say they don't need us.

15
00:00:39,472 --> 00:00:42,375
Isn't there anyone
better suited to be the director?

16
00:00:42,442 --> 00:00:44,010
What musical?

17
00:00:44,077 --> 00:00:46,279
The one that popular actress
Yuika Shiki is in.

18
00:00:46,346 --> 00:00:47,247
This one.

19
00:00:47,313 --> 00:00:48,314
He's in the musical?

20
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:50,050
No. Yuika Shiki.

21
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:51,718
What?

22
00:00:52,385 --> 00:00:53,386
TICKETS RESERVED

23
00:00:53,453 --> 00:00:55,221
I got them! Yes!

24
00:00:55,288 --> 00:00:57,257
Yes! Dr. Daimon, I got them!

25
00:00:57,323 --> 00:00:58,725
- Front row!
- Shut up!

26
00:00:58,792 --> 00:01:02,529
Last year, everything was canceled
because of COVID.

27
00:01:02,595 --> 00:01:04,197
Now, I can finally see Shiki!

28
00:01:04,264 --> 00:01:05,999
Look! It's Yuika Shiki!

29
00:01:06,066 --> 00:01:07,067
<i>NATALIE</i>

30
00:01:07,133 --> 00:01:08,168
I'm talking about this.

31
00:01:08,234 --> 00:01:10,570
Yuika Shiki? I think…

32
00:01:10,637 --> 00:01:14,207
there's a VIP patient
by that name hospitalized today.

33
00:01:14,274 --> 00:01:16,509
You mean Yuika Shiki is a VIP patient?

34
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:19,079
I don't know any of the details.

35
00:01:19,879 --> 00:01:21,047
I'm going to OR.

36
00:01:21,114 --> 00:01:22,949
Dr. Daimon, do you know anything?

37
00:01:23,016 --> 00:01:24,451
I don't know anything!

38
00:01:28,288 --> 00:01:30,523
I want to return to rehearsals quickly.

39
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:33,560
I must be in top condition by next month.

40
00:01:33,626 --> 00:01:34,861
Certainly.

41
00:01:34,928 --> 00:01:38,098
And absolutely make it certain
that the media doesn't know I'm here.

42
00:01:38,164 --> 00:01:39,432
Certainly.

43
00:01:39,499 --> 00:01:40,867
We'll take care of it.

44
00:01:52,645 --> 00:01:53,680
Wait.

45
00:01:54,347 --> 00:01:56,616
Aren't you that lady in the musical?

46
00:01:57,150 --> 00:01:58,051
Are you sick?

47
00:01:58,118 --> 00:01:59,152
Dr. Daimon!

48
00:01:59,219 --> 00:02:00,954
If you need surgery, let me do it.

49
00:02:01,654 --> 00:02:04,457
- I'm really good.
- What's wrong with you? That's rude!

50
00:02:04,524 --> 00:02:06,092
- I'm really good.
- Get out!

51
00:02:07,093 --> 00:02:08,761
I'm sorry about that.

52
00:02:11,097 --> 00:02:14,534
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of a maverick woman doctor.</i>

53
00:02:15,902 --> 00:02:17,537
<i>2021.</i>

54
00:02:18,204 --> 00:02:21,374
<i>The ravages</i>
<i>of a once-in-a-century pandemic…</i>

55
00:02:21,441 --> 00:02:24,043
<i>have devastated</i>
<i>the world's medical systems.</i>

56
00:02:25,211 --> 00:02:26,813
<i>With the might of a cornered animal,</i>

57
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:28,815
<i>Japan's medical universities</i>

58
00:02:29,382 --> 00:02:32,552
<i>have somehow weathered the storm.</i>

59
00:02:32,619 --> 00:02:35,255
We will now begin today's conference.

60
00:02:35,321 --> 00:02:38,458
The first case is Yuika Shiki, age 35.

61
00:02:38,958 --> 00:02:41,995
Squamous cell carcinoma
of the thyroid, stage 4B.

62
00:02:42,061 --> 00:02:44,464
I should have known! It's her!

63
00:02:44,531 --> 00:02:45,598
You must be kidding!

64
00:02:46,366 --> 00:02:48,601
Yuika Shiki has thyroid cancer?

65
00:02:48,668 --> 00:02:50,270
The tumor is huge!

66
00:02:50,336 --> 00:02:51,337
Out of the way!

67
00:02:53,439 --> 00:02:56,242
It's permeated the recurrent
laryngeal nerve and trachea.

68
00:02:56,309 --> 00:02:59,846
This situation is critical!
We must operate immediately!

69
00:02:59,913 --> 00:03:02,248
There is no need for you to operate.

70
00:03:02,315 --> 00:03:03,483
What?

71
00:03:03,550 --> 00:03:05,585
This thyroid cancer will be treated

72
00:03:05,652 --> 00:03:07,987
with chemical surgery.

73
00:03:09,355 --> 00:03:10,523
Chemical surgery?

74
00:03:10,590 --> 00:03:12,525
Surgery without cutting open the patient.

75
00:03:13,159 --> 00:03:14,160
In other words,

76
00:03:14,227 --> 00:03:16,062
it's in the hands of the internists.

77
00:03:16,129 --> 00:03:18,364
This is already beyond
the scope of surgery.

78
00:03:18,431 --> 00:03:21,034
However, using BNCT chemical surgery,

79
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:23,803
that is, boron neutron capture therapy,

80
00:03:24,304 --> 00:03:28,408
boron medication administered via IV
is absorbed by the cancer cells.

81
00:03:28,474 --> 00:03:31,110
Then the area is irradiated with neutrons,

82
00:03:31,177 --> 00:03:33,046
selectively destroying the cancerous cells

83
00:03:33,112 --> 00:03:36,649
with minimal harm to the normal cells.

84
00:03:36,716 --> 00:03:38,151
In this case,

85
00:03:38,218 --> 00:03:40,620
the best treatment
is through non-surgical methods.

86
00:03:40,687 --> 00:03:41,788
- Indeed.
- Indeed.

87
00:03:41,854 --> 00:03:45,291
But to make sure
it has been entirely removed,

88
00:03:45,358 --> 00:03:46,960
we should consider surgical methods.

89
00:03:47,026 --> 00:03:49,062
Internal Medicine will decide
the treatment.

90
00:03:49,128 --> 00:03:52,999
The Surgery Department will only do
surgeries we deem necessary.

91
00:03:55,034 --> 00:03:56,336
Is there something else?

92
00:03:56,903 --> 00:03:57,870
No.

93
00:04:01,841 --> 00:04:03,176
<i>Dr. Ebina.</i>

94
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:06,012
<i>Hey, Dr. Ebina.</i>

95
00:04:06,079 --> 00:04:07,447
Branch Director Hiruma.

96
00:04:07,513 --> 00:04:10,483
<i>Don't you dare let Internal Medicine</i>
<i>steal away</i>

97
00:04:10,550 --> 00:04:12,218
<i>this important VIP patient.</i>

98
00:04:12,285 --> 00:04:13,486
<i>Right, Dr. Ebina?</i>

99
00:04:13,553 --> 00:04:16,723
<i>You call yourself Director of Surgery?</i>
<i>Well, Dr. Ebina?</i>

100
00:04:16,789 --> 00:04:17,790
<i>Dr. Ebina.</i>

101
00:04:18,324 --> 00:04:19,559
<i>What's with you, Dr. Ebina?</i>

102
00:04:19,626 --> 00:04:21,294
With all due respect,

103
00:04:21,361 --> 00:04:24,063
I'm against this treatment method.

104
00:04:24,130 --> 00:04:25,898
Until now,

105
00:04:25,965 --> 00:04:28,534
we in the Surgery Department have treated

106
00:04:28,601 --> 00:04:30,203
many VIP patients with surgery.

107
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:31,537
Dr. Ebina,

108
00:04:31,604 --> 00:04:34,674
what's important
aren't the treatments of the past,

109
00:04:34,741 --> 00:04:36,776
but the treatments of the future.

110
00:04:36,843 --> 00:04:40,546
For important patients like Yuika Shiki,

111
00:04:40,613 --> 00:04:43,116
next-generation treatments should be used!

112
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:47,520
<i>Do you want to start</i>
<i>from the bottom again, Dr. Ebina?</i>

113
00:04:49,289 --> 00:04:51,658
But without everything we've done before,

114
00:04:51,724 --> 00:04:53,960
there wouldn't be any future, right?

115
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:57,630
Just calling it "next-generation"
doesn't mean it's any good!

116
00:04:57,697 --> 00:04:59,532
Dr. Ebina, you're so right!

117
00:04:59,599 --> 00:05:03,136
Hey, how many times
will you irradiate with BNCT?

118
00:05:03,202 --> 00:05:05,271
Why don't you just calm down, Dr. Ebina?

119
00:05:12,845 --> 00:05:14,714
You know what I think?

120
00:05:14,781 --> 00:05:18,418
You internists just don't like it
when we surgeons cure patients.

121
00:05:19,218 --> 00:05:21,988
All you think about
is improving your own status.

122
00:05:22,055 --> 00:05:24,924
Like I said,
how many times will you irradiate

123
00:05:24,991 --> 00:05:26,459
- with BNCT?
- Dr. Daimon, get a clue!

124
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:28,394
Scary…

125
00:05:28,461 --> 00:05:31,130
Dr. Ebina, take back what you said.

126
00:05:31,197 --> 00:05:34,767
We have chosen the best treatment
for this thyroid cancer.

127
00:05:34,834 --> 00:05:36,469
No, I'm not taking it back.

128
00:05:36,536 --> 00:05:38,104
You internists,

129
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:41,274
you're a hopeless bunch
led by this sham of a director!

130
00:05:41,874 --> 00:05:43,242
We don't need you internists!

131
00:05:50,483 --> 00:05:51,884
What? Branch Director Hiruma?

132
00:05:53,052 --> 00:05:54,120
Branch Director Hiruma?

133
00:05:57,490 --> 00:05:59,125
Sorry about…

134
00:06:00,193 --> 00:06:01,094
what I just said.

135
00:06:02,628 --> 00:06:04,130
I don't mind.

136
00:06:05,064 --> 00:06:06,833
- What?
- Go right ahead.

137
00:06:08,301 --> 00:06:10,269
Treat her with surgery!

138
00:06:10,803 --> 00:06:11,771
However…

139
00:06:13,072 --> 00:06:18,411
you have insulted the methods
of treatment we've used until now.

140
00:06:20,313 --> 00:06:23,082
So if Yuika Shiki
is not cured via surgery,

141
00:06:23,950 --> 00:06:25,685
you must pay the consequences.

142
00:06:27,387 --> 00:06:28,621
The consequences?

143
00:06:30,857 --> 00:06:32,759
Submit your resignation!

144
00:06:36,095 --> 00:06:37,096
Dr. Daimon,

145
00:06:37,163 --> 00:06:38,498
it will work out, right?

146
00:06:42,402 --> 00:06:45,138
And if we cure her through surgery…

147
00:06:46,539 --> 00:06:47,640
what will you do?

148
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:49,876
If that happens,

149
00:06:51,511 --> 00:06:53,413
I will resign.

150
00:06:56,616 --> 00:06:57,617
Okay.

151
00:06:58,117 --> 00:06:59,385
Okay.

152
00:06:59,452 --> 00:07:00,787
<i>Meanwhile,</i>

153
00:07:00,853 --> 00:07:03,423
<i>this freelance maverick doctor</i>

154
00:07:03,489 --> 00:07:07,427
<i>who was never attached</i>
<i>to any hospital returned.</i>

155
00:07:07,493 --> 00:07:08,461
Dr. Daimon!

156
00:07:09,028 --> 00:07:10,463
It will work out, right?

157
00:07:10,530 --> 00:07:12,532
<i>She hates groups,</i>

158
00:07:13,332 --> 00:07:15,868
<i>she hates authority,</i>

159
00:07:15,935 --> 00:07:17,703
<i>and she hates restrictions.</i>

160
00:07:18,471 --> 00:07:21,574
<i>Her weapons are</i>
<i>her specialty license and her skill</i>

161
00:07:21,641 --> 00:07:23,042
<i>to work her way up.</i>

162
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:24,243
Let's do this.

163
00:07:24,310 --> 00:07:25,411
I look forward to it.

164
00:07:26,145 --> 00:07:27,413
Let's do it!

165
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:29,148
Let's do this, surgeons!

166
00:07:29,215 --> 00:07:31,517
Let's cure Yuika Shiki with surgery!

167
00:07:31,584 --> 00:07:32,785
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

168
00:07:37,757 --> 00:07:40,092
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

169
00:07:40,159 --> 00:07:43,162
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

170
00:08:12,558 --> 00:08:14,060
Don't underestimate surgery!

171
00:08:14,126 --> 00:08:17,296
We've got the ultimate weapon.
Dr. Daimon! She'll cut up anything!

172
00:08:20,199 --> 00:08:21,834
Director Ebina stopped!

173
00:08:28,140 --> 00:08:29,275
Go ahead.

174
00:08:31,777 --> 00:08:32,645
Excuse us.

175
00:08:36,282 --> 00:08:37,283
Ms. Shiki.

176
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:40,686
I'm Director of Surgery, Takashi Ebina.

177
00:08:40,753 --> 00:08:42,855
I've seen many of your performances.

178
00:08:42,922 --> 00:08:44,590
It's an honor to meet you.

179
00:08:45,558 --> 00:08:47,226
As Director of Surgery,

180
00:08:47,293 --> 00:08:50,396
I will explain your surgery.

181
00:08:50,463 --> 00:08:54,667
Are you sure you want to let
the Surgery Department operate?

182
00:08:54,734 --> 00:08:56,135
It won't be a problem.

183
00:08:56,202 --> 00:08:57,637
For this patient,

184
00:08:57,703 --> 00:09:01,707
chemical surgery is 100%
the most appropriate method.

185
00:09:03,809 --> 00:09:07,813
But the Surgery Department
doesn't understand why.

186
00:09:08,681 --> 00:09:10,683
I won't be operated on.

187
00:09:11,250 --> 00:09:12,685
Why not?

188
00:09:12,752 --> 00:09:14,387
If I'm operated on,

189
00:09:14,453 --> 00:09:17,623
it will take time to recover
and it will delay rehearsals.

190
00:09:17,690 --> 00:09:19,025
What's more,

191
00:09:19,091 --> 00:09:20,226
I am an actress.

192
00:09:21,093 --> 00:09:22,495
If I'm operated on,

193
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:23,729
it will leave a scar.

194
00:09:24,463 --> 00:09:25,731
Well, a little.

195
00:09:27,099 --> 00:09:29,101
I won't have a scar on my neck!

196
00:09:29,735 --> 00:09:31,137
I came to Totei University

197
00:09:31,203 --> 00:09:33,839
because I heard I could be cured
without surgery!

198
00:09:35,141 --> 00:09:37,310
Hey, out of the way.

199
00:09:37,376 --> 00:09:39,378
- Excuse me!
- Dr. Daimon is here!

200
00:09:39,445 --> 00:09:40,913
She's here!

201
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:43,516
If you leave it to her,
she'll do perfect surgery.

202
00:09:43,583 --> 00:09:46,385
Any scar will be absolutely tiny.
Right, Dr. Daimon?

203
00:09:46,452 --> 00:09:47,420
What?

204
00:09:47,486 --> 00:09:50,656
I refuse to be operated on by that doctor.

205
00:09:52,825 --> 00:09:53,826
Why?

206
00:09:54,393 --> 00:09:58,397
I was repulsed by how she said,
"If you need surgery, let me do it."

207
00:09:59,465 --> 00:10:01,667
That's the arrogance of a doctor.

208
00:10:03,002 --> 00:10:04,637
What are you doing, Dr. Daimon?

209
00:10:04,704 --> 00:10:06,472
Apologize to her.

210
00:10:06,539 --> 00:10:08,174
What a ridiculous statement.

211
00:10:08,741 --> 00:10:10,943
What if you made a mistake?

212
00:10:11,010 --> 00:10:12,812
I wouldn't worry about that.

213
00:10:12,878 --> 00:10:14,814
Give her your usual line.

214
00:10:14,880 --> 00:10:15,881
Hurry up.

215
00:10:15,948 --> 00:10:18,084
Get over here.

216
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:22,755
- I…
- Yes, that one.

217
00:10:26,525 --> 00:10:27,727
won't operate.

218
00:10:29,629 --> 00:10:31,464
- Dr. Daimon…
- You won't operate?

219
00:10:31,530 --> 00:10:33,399
What do you mean?

220
00:10:33,466 --> 00:10:35,668
You want them to do chemical surgery?

221
00:10:37,003 --> 00:10:37,970
Sure, why not?

222
00:10:38,037 --> 00:10:39,805
- Wait!
- Hey!

223
00:10:43,576 --> 00:10:44,677
"Sure, why not?"

224
00:10:46,178 --> 00:10:48,314
As arrogant as ever.

225
00:10:52,151 --> 00:10:53,319
What will I do now?

226
00:10:54,253 --> 00:10:56,122
So…

227
00:10:56,188 --> 00:10:59,191
she refused surgery.

228
00:10:59,692 --> 00:11:03,329
Dr. Ebina is in real trouble now.

229
00:11:04,096 --> 00:11:06,098
This is what happens

230
00:11:06,165 --> 00:11:08,367
when he relies on Demon
and makes these stupid bets.

231
00:11:08,434 --> 00:11:11,337
I heard that Yuika Shiki
is difficult to deal with,

232
00:11:11,404 --> 00:11:14,106
so it makes sense
she and Dr. Daimon had a conflict.

233
00:11:14,173 --> 00:11:18,577
I heard rumors that she's a playgirl
and goes through men like crazy.

234
00:11:18,644 --> 00:11:20,980
Well, as for me…

235
00:11:21,047 --> 00:11:24,283
But people don't mind.
She is internationally famous, after all.

236
00:11:24,784 --> 00:11:27,086
I heard tickets sell out instantly.

237
00:11:27,153 --> 00:11:28,154
Really?

238
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:32,124
But if worse comes to worst,

239
00:11:32,191 --> 00:11:35,594
there's really only one choice
for the next Director of Surgery.

240
00:11:35,661 --> 00:11:38,330
Such a pity getting cancer
before a big show.

241
00:11:38,397 --> 00:11:39,799
I hope she recovers in time.

242
00:11:40,900 --> 00:11:42,268
<i>Second floor.</i>

243
00:11:46,605 --> 00:11:49,375
See, I'm still all alone.

244
00:11:49,942 --> 00:11:51,911
I wish Hara would come back.

245
00:11:53,312 --> 00:11:54,680
Why did you…

246
00:11:55,381 --> 00:11:59,185
get carried away and pick
a fight with Internal Medicine?

247
00:12:00,186 --> 00:12:01,787
I'll apologize to them

248
00:12:01,854 --> 00:12:04,090
and take back the promise to resign.

249
00:12:05,524 --> 00:12:08,160
It's too late for that, you moron!

250
00:12:08,227 --> 00:12:09,261
I see…

251
00:12:09,328 --> 00:12:12,598
Don't you dare do anything
to ruin Surgery's reputation!

252
00:12:12,665 --> 00:12:16,502
But I finally became a director
after the humiliation of being a nobody.

253
00:12:18,204 --> 00:12:20,072
- I'm going to apologize!
- Stop!

254
00:12:21,140 --> 00:12:23,109
Don't lose your head!

255
00:12:23,175 --> 00:12:24,009
But…

256
00:12:24,076 --> 00:12:27,847
- What are you getting so hasty for?
- Sorry.

257
00:12:27,913 --> 00:12:28,848
Don't worry.

258
00:12:30,015 --> 00:12:31,784
You have me behind you.

259
00:12:31,851 --> 00:12:34,120
Thank you, Branch Director Hiruma.

260
00:12:34,186 --> 00:12:35,387
- Excuse me.
- Come in.

261
00:12:36,889 --> 00:12:37,757
Thank you.

262
00:12:38,390 --> 00:12:40,526
Your tea, Acting Hospital Director Hiruma.

263
00:12:41,961 --> 00:12:45,431
What? When did you become
Acting Hospital Director?

264
00:12:45,498 --> 00:12:47,166
I will be soon.

265
00:12:47,233 --> 00:12:48,334
Okay…

266
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:49,602
- Yui.
- Yes?

267
00:12:49,668 --> 00:12:51,203
Can you call me that again?

268
00:12:51,270 --> 00:12:53,439
Acting Hospital Director Hiruma.

269
00:12:55,174 --> 00:12:56,142
Listen.

270
00:12:57,710 --> 00:12:58,811
Entice Dr. Daimon…

271
00:13:00,179 --> 00:13:01,614
as much as you can.

272
00:13:02,715 --> 00:13:04,650
She obviously wants to operate.

273
00:13:05,151 --> 00:13:07,553
- Right?
- Yes, but how?

274
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:09,288
Feed her delicious meat.

275
00:13:10,089 --> 00:13:11,357
Out of your own pocket.

276
00:13:15,227 --> 00:13:17,797
Dr. Hachisuka, as I told you before,

277
00:13:17,863 --> 00:13:21,467
that near-future medical treatment
project I've been working on

278
00:13:21,534 --> 00:13:23,035
is finally getting started.

279
00:13:24,170 --> 00:13:25,738
This is the project to prevent…

280
00:13:26,372 --> 00:13:28,541
the future collapse of medical systems

281
00:13:28,607 --> 00:13:31,043
based on the lessons learned
from COVID, right?

282
00:13:31,877 --> 00:13:35,114
We must also officially appoint
a project leader.

283
00:13:35,181 --> 00:13:37,550
Next-generation politics needs…

284
00:13:38,083 --> 00:13:39,385
next-generation medicine.

285
00:13:39,451 --> 00:13:41,387
Currently at Totei University,

286
00:13:41,453 --> 00:13:45,024
we are using a treatment emblematic
of next-generation medicine,

287
00:13:45,090 --> 00:13:48,194
BNCT chemical surgery,

288
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:51,931
to treat the stage actress, Yuika Shiki.

289
00:13:51,997 --> 00:13:53,165
Oh, wow…

290
00:13:53,232 --> 00:13:55,568
You're really something, Dr. Hachisuka.

291
00:13:55,634 --> 00:13:59,405
She's the perfect patient to prove
the effectiveness of chemical surgery.

292
00:13:59,471 --> 00:14:03,209
I swear we'll achieve success
and live up to your expectations.

293
00:14:04,210 --> 00:14:05,444
Oh…

294
00:14:05,511 --> 00:14:07,813
Naturally,
since this is personal information,

295
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:09,415
keep it under wraps.

296
00:14:09,481 --> 00:14:10,683
Yuika Shiki

297
00:14:10,749 --> 00:14:13,752
is about to begin starring
in an international production, right?

298
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:15,654
Will she be ready in time?

299
00:14:16,455 --> 00:14:17,690
It won't be a problem.

300
00:14:17,756 --> 00:14:20,159
Leave it to me, Hachisuka.

301
00:14:20,226 --> 00:14:21,293
But…

302
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:24,663
treating her hastily
won't come to any good.

303
00:14:26,498 --> 00:14:30,603
Don't you think it's better
to spend plenty of time on it?

304
00:14:31,170 --> 00:14:32,371
Spend plenty of time?

305
00:14:35,741 --> 00:14:36,842
One's life is…

306
00:14:37,610 --> 00:14:40,079
more important than the stage, you know.

307
00:14:53,058 --> 00:14:55,561
So she doesn't want a scar on her neck.

308
00:14:55,628 --> 00:14:58,430
Since she's a stage actress,
I can understand that.

309
00:14:59,098 --> 00:15:00,666
In particular, Yuika Shiki.

310
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:02,201
Apparently, she cares

311
00:15:02,268 --> 00:15:04,536
for her throat
almost as much as her own life.

312
00:15:04,603 --> 00:15:07,006
With it in her trachea
and recurrent laryngeal nerve,

313
00:15:07,072 --> 00:15:08,307
it's hard to operate.

314
00:15:08,374 --> 00:15:09,275
Yes.

315
00:15:09,341 --> 00:15:11,677
How can you talk like that?

316
00:15:11,744 --> 00:15:14,280
You've succeeded at numerous surgeries

317
00:15:14,346 --> 00:15:16,248
that were considered impossible.

318
00:15:16,315 --> 00:15:17,583
What are you doing here?

319
00:15:17,650 --> 00:15:19,551
I wanted to do <i>yakiniku</i> with you.

320
00:15:19,618 --> 00:15:21,053
Okay, the vegetables are ready.

321
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:23,522
Thanks for taking care of everything.

322
00:15:23,589 --> 00:15:25,391
No problem. I bought lots of meat, too.

323
00:15:25,457 --> 00:15:28,360
Eat heartily, drink heavily, and operate.

324
00:15:28,427 --> 00:15:31,730
- This is cheap meat!
- What? Oh, you're right!

325
00:15:31,797 --> 00:15:34,033
I'll eat and drink, but I won't operate.

326
00:15:34,633 --> 00:15:35,868
You talk like that,

327
00:15:35,935 --> 00:15:39,405
but you'll just steal her away
while Internal Medicine is treating her.

328
00:15:39,471 --> 00:15:40,806
I won't.

329
00:15:40,873 --> 00:15:42,574
- Do it. Please.
- I won't.

330
00:15:42,641 --> 00:15:45,144
I was asked to assist
with that chemical surgery.

331
00:15:45,210 --> 00:15:46,946
Is that right? See you there.

332
00:15:47,012 --> 00:15:49,148
It's not like you'll be there!

333
00:15:49,214 --> 00:15:51,984
- And Dr. Jonouchi, we were partners!
- Since when?

334
00:15:52,051 --> 00:15:54,286
Okay, I'll put on the meat.

335
00:15:54,353 --> 00:15:56,422
All right!

336
00:15:59,325 --> 00:16:01,226
Cheers!

337
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:02,795
Sorry, I'm a little late.

338
00:16:02,861 --> 00:16:04,096
Where did that come from?

339
00:16:04,163 --> 00:16:05,564
- Hey, that's 230 yen.
- What?

340
00:16:05,631 --> 00:16:06,699
Pay up.

341
00:16:06,765 --> 00:16:08,000
NEUTRON IRRADIATION ROOM

342
00:16:08,067 --> 00:16:09,702
I'll administer midazolam.

343
00:16:10,269 --> 00:16:12,771
- You'll become slightly drowsy.
- Okay.

344
00:16:15,341 --> 00:16:16,442
How long is irradiation?

345
00:16:17,209 --> 00:16:21,447
Normally, it's 30 to 60 minutes.
This time, it will be for 60 minutes.

346
00:16:21,513 --> 00:16:23,282
I see. And the collimator?

347
00:16:23,349 --> 00:16:26,118
- Of course, it's ready.
- Okay.

348
00:16:26,185 --> 00:16:29,922
Dr. Daimon, what are you doing here?
This isn't a surgery.

349
00:16:29,989 --> 00:16:31,657
How much midazolam?

350
00:16:31,724 --> 00:16:32,791
One cc at first,

351
00:16:32,858 --> 00:16:35,561
gradually administered and more of it
is added depending on the effect.

352
00:16:35,627 --> 00:16:38,097
We don't want her moving
during irradiation.

353
00:16:38,664 --> 00:16:40,265
Aren't you listening? Get out.

354
00:16:40,332 --> 00:16:41,867
Okay, let's begin!

355
00:16:44,236 --> 00:16:45,971
You're not in charge here!

356
00:16:46,538 --> 00:16:48,340
She acts like she's operating.

357
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:56,315
Commence irradiation!

358
00:16:56,382 --> 00:16:57,616
We know that.

359
00:17:06,725 --> 00:17:10,029
Is she receiving five grams
of boron medication during irradiation?

360
00:17:10,095 --> 00:17:13,599
Of course. The dose
is 12 gray equivalent, right?

361
00:17:13,665 --> 00:17:14,500
Right.

362
00:17:14,566 --> 00:17:15,667
How about hydration?

363
00:17:15,734 --> 00:17:18,103
250 saline solution IV per hour.

364
00:17:23,042 --> 00:17:25,277
Chemical surgery is magnificent.

365
00:17:26,211 --> 00:17:28,480
Operating without opening up the patient.

366
00:17:28,547 --> 00:17:31,817
This truly is medical treatment
fit for the Reiwa era.

367
00:17:34,653 --> 00:17:37,923
And Dr. Daimon is also magnificent.

368
00:17:37,990 --> 00:17:40,926
She crosses the barrier between surgery

369
00:17:40,993 --> 00:17:43,429
and internal medicine,
looking toward the future.

370
00:17:43,495 --> 00:17:46,765
She's wasted as just a plain surgeon.

371
00:17:52,604 --> 00:17:54,373
"What's so important?"

372
00:17:55,207 --> 00:17:56,275
"Revolution?"

373
00:17:57,176 --> 00:17:58,110
Excuse me.

374
00:17:59,578 --> 00:18:01,080
How are you feeling?

375
00:18:02,548 --> 00:18:05,217
Aren't you a surgeon, Dr. Daimon?

376
00:18:06,318 --> 00:18:08,554
I am a freelance surgeon.

377
00:18:09,588 --> 00:18:12,724
I bet you're actually a fan of mine,
aren't you?

378
00:18:13,258 --> 00:18:14,126
What?

379
00:18:14,693 --> 00:18:15,794
I can tell.

380
00:18:16,562 --> 00:18:17,830
Want my autograph?

381
00:18:17,896 --> 00:18:19,231
I'm not a fan.

382
00:18:20,666 --> 00:18:21,733
Excuse me.

383
00:18:22,468 --> 00:18:24,803
Ms. Shiki, you have a visitor.

384
00:18:24,870 --> 00:18:26,371
Excuse me.

385
00:18:27,206 --> 00:18:28,607
Yuika!

386
00:18:28,674 --> 00:18:30,509
How are you feeling?

387
00:18:30,576 --> 00:18:33,112
I'm sorry I couldn't visit sooner.

388
00:18:34,246 --> 00:18:35,414
Oh, you made it.

389
00:18:35,481 --> 00:18:36,482
Thank you.

390
00:18:36,548 --> 00:18:38,217
Everyone is worried about you.

391
00:18:38,750 --> 00:18:40,786
That's Kaede, one of the co-stars.

392
00:18:40,853 --> 00:18:44,990
- She's nearly as popular as Ms. Shiki.
- Really?

393
00:18:45,057 --> 00:18:46,725
I'll be out of the hospital soon.

394
00:18:46,792 --> 00:18:48,327
Take care of things until then.

395
00:18:48,393 --> 00:18:50,162
Make sure you're all better.

396
00:18:50,229 --> 00:18:52,865
I mean, you're the only one
suited to play the lead.

397
00:18:54,233 --> 00:18:57,803
I get the feeling there's some
silent tension between them.

398
00:18:57,870 --> 00:19:01,273
By the way, have you seen the news?
It's quite the story.

399
00:19:04,443 --> 00:19:06,512
STAGE ACTRESS YUIKA SHIKI
HOSPITALIZED FOR CANCER

400
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:09,982
Isn't this awful?

401
00:19:10,048 --> 00:19:11,350
Who could have leaked it?

402
00:19:11,416 --> 00:19:12,684
Let me see that!

403
00:19:13,185 --> 00:19:15,621
Ms. Shiki, are you all right?

404
00:19:15,687 --> 00:19:17,122
Please lie down a while.

405
00:19:18,757 --> 00:19:20,726
It's rehearsal time, so I'll be going.

406
00:19:21,260 --> 00:19:22,528
Yuika,

407
00:19:22,594 --> 00:19:24,596
don't push yourself too hard.

408
00:19:28,634 --> 00:19:29,968
I'll tilt the bed back.

409
00:19:34,940 --> 00:19:36,909
She totally wants to steal the lead role.

410
00:19:36,975 --> 00:19:39,444
Competition for the lead role
sure is brutal.

411
00:19:40,712 --> 00:19:41,914
Compared to that,

412
00:19:41,980 --> 00:19:45,551
the battle between directors
was settled pretty quickly, wasn't it?

413
00:19:46,185 --> 00:19:49,254
Results of the chemical surgery
have been very good.

414
00:19:49,321 --> 00:19:52,191
At this rate, Dr. Ebina will get the boot.

415
00:19:56,261 --> 00:19:57,095
What?

416
00:20:01,266 --> 00:20:02,568
Excuse me!

417
00:20:03,268 --> 00:20:04,203
Ms. Shiki,

418
00:20:04,269 --> 00:20:05,804
don't worry!

419
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:09,374
I'll speak to them and convince them
to put you on stage…

420
00:20:16,582 --> 00:20:18,350
Excuse me.

421
00:20:19,685 --> 00:20:20,652
She's gone!

422
00:20:21,853 --> 00:20:23,989
Do you know where Ms. Shiki is?

423
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:26,058
Ms. Shiki is in the children's playroom.

424
00:20:26,858 --> 00:20:28,193
The playroom…

425
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:29,761
Thank you.

426
00:21:15,741 --> 00:21:16,908
Thank you.

427
00:21:17,509 --> 00:21:20,545
I didn't expect Dr. Daimon
to be a fan of this kind of thing.

428
00:21:21,546 --> 00:21:23,248
Have you gotten all better?

429
00:21:23,315 --> 00:21:24,916
Yes, I'm just fine.

430
00:21:24,983 --> 00:21:26,418
I'm all better.

431
00:21:30,122 --> 00:21:32,124
Ms. Shiki, are you all right?

432
00:21:32,190 --> 00:21:34,626
You look pale. Let's return to your room.

433
00:21:34,693 --> 00:21:35,694
Okay.

434
00:21:35,761 --> 00:21:38,497
Since news got out that I'm here,

435
00:21:38,563 --> 00:21:41,767
I wanted to do anything
that I could do to help.

436
00:21:42,267 --> 00:21:44,303
Thank you. Let's go.

437
00:21:44,369 --> 00:21:45,370
Okay.

438
00:21:46,705 --> 00:21:50,375
I'm thrilled
I could hear her sing this close.

439
00:21:51,610 --> 00:21:53,378
This is the real Yuika Shiki.

440
00:21:54,813 --> 00:21:56,548
Spreading happiness through song.

441
00:21:57,582 --> 00:21:58,950
Like a real Venus.

442
00:22:00,018 --> 00:22:01,453
I bet you think so, too.

443
00:22:03,288 --> 00:22:05,757
Your face and words are scary.

444
00:22:05,824 --> 00:22:07,959
That chemical surgery works well.

445
00:22:09,094 --> 00:22:10,128
I'm glad.

446
00:22:11,163 --> 00:22:13,432
I'm happy as long as Yuika gets better.

447
00:22:13,498 --> 00:22:15,534
Even if it's not me who does it

448
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:17,169
and even if I lose my job.

449
00:22:17,736 --> 00:22:19,171
None of it matters.

450
00:22:19,905 --> 00:22:21,206
I have no…

451
00:22:25,610 --> 00:22:27,779
VIP ROOM A

452
00:22:27,846 --> 00:22:29,648
You seem tired.

453
00:22:29,715 --> 00:22:31,516
Don't push yourself too much yet.

454
00:22:32,150 --> 00:22:33,185
Okay.

455
00:22:34,286 --> 00:22:35,620
Ms. Yuika Shiki,

456
00:22:35,687 --> 00:22:38,924
though you are receiving treatment,

457
00:22:38,990 --> 00:22:40,992
you sang for the other patients.

458
00:22:41,059 --> 00:22:42,594
On behalf of the hospital,

459
00:22:43,662 --> 00:22:44,696
allow me to thank you.

460
00:22:45,697 --> 00:22:47,099
Dr. Hachisuka…

461
00:22:49,768 --> 00:22:50,602
Well…

462
00:22:51,570 --> 00:22:53,438
Thanks to chemical surgery,

463
00:22:53,939 --> 00:22:56,742
the tumors have clearly shrunk.

464
00:22:56,808 --> 00:22:57,809
However,

465
00:22:58,343 --> 00:23:01,246
to achieve a 100% cure,

466
00:23:01,313 --> 00:23:03,815
let's consider second irradiation.

467
00:23:04,483 --> 00:23:05,550
A second one?

468
00:23:07,486 --> 00:23:09,955
I will make it in time to perform, right?

469
00:23:10,455 --> 00:23:12,290
We'll do our very best.

470
00:23:12,357 --> 00:23:13,892
I would appreciate it.

471
00:23:14,860 --> 00:23:17,362
I want to be in this musical
even if it kills me.

472
00:23:18,397 --> 00:23:19,598
I want to sing!

473
00:23:22,134 --> 00:23:23,402
"Even if it kills me?"

474
00:23:23,468 --> 00:23:24,803
Don't talk like that.

475
00:23:25,437 --> 00:23:28,974
The priority now is to cure
the singer, Yuika Shiki,

476
00:23:29,040 --> 00:23:31,476
of her disease.

477
00:23:33,512 --> 00:23:34,579
Goodbye.

478
00:23:39,551 --> 00:23:40,552
Hey.

479
00:23:41,086 --> 00:23:42,921
Are you really trying to cure her?

480
00:23:44,623 --> 00:23:47,392
It sounds like
you're trying to waste time.

481
00:23:47,459 --> 00:23:50,395
Let us cure the patient together.

482
00:24:05,644 --> 00:24:10,315
<i>NATALIE</i>

483
00:24:13,785 --> 00:24:16,621
YUIKA SHIKI ENTERTAINING MEDICAL WORKERS

484
00:24:24,229 --> 00:24:25,330
- Hey.
- What?

485
00:24:25,397 --> 00:24:26,665
- What's up, Ms. Daimon?
- What?

486
00:24:26,731 --> 00:24:28,533
- Is something bothering you?
- What?

487
00:24:28,600 --> 00:24:31,269
That chemical surgery is working, right?

488
00:24:31,336 --> 00:24:32,871
I know, but…

489
00:24:32,938 --> 00:24:35,574
Yuika sure has a beautiful singing voice.

490
00:24:36,908 --> 00:24:38,176
<i>Last year,</i>

491
00:24:38,677 --> 00:24:40,378
when COVID was at its peak,

492
00:24:40,445 --> 00:24:44,282
she sang for medical staff
many times to cheer them up.

493
00:24:45,584 --> 00:24:49,421
She also did lots of free streaming
for people stuck at home

494
00:24:49,488 --> 00:24:53,124
to add some light
to people's lives with song.

495
00:24:53,191 --> 00:24:54,693
I see.

496
00:24:54,759 --> 00:24:57,996
Even her own shows got canceled,

497
00:24:58,063 --> 00:25:00,565
so it must have been tough
for her as well.

498
00:25:11,776 --> 00:25:13,311
What is it?

499
00:25:14,479 --> 00:25:16,014
What?

500
00:25:16,081 --> 00:25:17,315
I realized something!

501
00:25:17,382 --> 00:25:19,985
- I completed my hand!
- What?

502
00:25:20,051 --> 00:25:22,220
<i>Menchin!</i> No way!

503
00:25:22,287 --> 00:25:23,522
What?

504
00:25:23,588 --> 00:25:25,690
I'm surprised you noticed.

505
00:25:31,396 --> 00:25:33,431
SURGERY BRANCH

506
00:25:33,498 --> 00:25:35,667
DEPARTMENT OF SURGERY

507
00:25:50,215 --> 00:25:51,182
RESIGNATION

508
00:25:55,487 --> 00:25:56,788
Give up my role?

509
00:25:57,289 --> 00:25:58,423
Wait a minute!

510
00:25:58,490 --> 00:26:02,360
The hospital told us that the treatment
would take some more time.

511
00:26:02,427 --> 00:26:05,330
If you push too hard,
it could hurt you later.

512
00:26:05,397 --> 00:26:06,731
I'm certain

513
00:26:06,798 --> 00:26:10,302
that Kaede will do just as good a job
at attracting audiences.

514
00:26:11,036 --> 00:26:12,704
I swear I'll be ready in time.

515
00:26:13,738 --> 00:26:15,173
Please wait a little longer.

516
00:26:16,074 --> 00:26:17,242
Please!

517
00:26:17,309 --> 00:26:19,244
We'll consider it, but…

518
00:26:19,311 --> 00:26:20,812
Yuika.

519
00:26:21,379 --> 00:26:24,049
Take your time and rest,
so you can get better.

520
00:26:25,917 --> 00:26:29,321
I'll do my best for you, Yuika.

521
00:26:31,523 --> 00:26:32,757
- Let's go.
- Okay.

522
00:26:33,258 --> 00:26:34,726
- Take care.
- Goodbye.

523
00:26:49,007 --> 00:26:51,042
Dr. Daimon, I beg you! Operate!

524
00:26:51,109 --> 00:26:53,278
I'm not saying this to save my neck!

525
00:26:54,813 --> 00:26:57,315
I want you to cure Yuika Shiki,
so she can perform.

526
00:26:58,617 --> 00:26:59,751
With your skills,

527
00:26:59,818 --> 00:27:01,453
I'm sure you can remove
her thyroid cancer.

528
00:27:02,253 --> 00:27:03,989
I won't do it.

529
00:27:04,055 --> 00:27:07,225
Then I'll convince her and operate myself!
Do you want that?

530
00:27:09,027 --> 00:27:10,362
What's with you?

531
00:27:10,428 --> 00:27:12,697
Where's your usual line,
"That will kill her?"

532
00:27:15,500 --> 00:27:17,602
I have nothing left to lose.

533
00:27:18,903 --> 00:27:20,538
This is all I can do for her.

534
00:27:23,308 --> 00:27:24,309
Dr. Daimon,

535
00:27:24,376 --> 00:27:27,012
my neck is on the chopping block.

536
00:27:29,981 --> 00:27:31,316
I won't let anyone's neck get cut.

537
00:27:33,418 --> 00:27:34,486
Okay?

538
00:27:38,523 --> 00:27:39,724
Dr. Daimon…

539
00:27:42,961 --> 00:27:44,562
Dr. Daimon!

540
00:27:45,664 --> 00:27:47,632
- Here are the test results.
- Thanks.

541
00:27:48,733 --> 00:27:52,103
Is it okay to run tests
without Internal Medicine's approval?

542
00:27:52,804 --> 00:27:53,972
Like I thought.

543
00:27:54,039 --> 00:27:55,006
What?

544
00:27:55,573 --> 00:27:57,208
- Thank you.
- What?

545
00:28:14,359 --> 00:28:15,727
Excuse me.

546
00:28:21,366 --> 00:28:26,771
I've always had confidence in my singing.

547
00:28:28,773 --> 00:28:31,242
There are many actresses prettier than me.

548
00:28:33,545 --> 00:28:35,180
But I could confidently say,

549
00:28:36,181 --> 00:28:37,549
"I can sing."

550
00:28:41,019 --> 00:28:44,622
It's the same with you,
isn't it, Dr. Daimon?

551
00:28:46,725 --> 00:28:49,327
You can say, "Let me operate,"

552
00:28:51,362 --> 00:28:53,465
because you're confident you can cure me.

553
00:28:59,504 --> 00:29:01,639
To be an actress in musicals,

554
00:29:01,706 --> 00:29:03,641
I've sacrificed a lot.

555
00:29:05,110 --> 00:29:08,179
I've had to leave
all the men I've dated as well.

556
00:29:09,380 --> 00:29:11,449
The press prints all kinds of lies.

557
00:29:13,852 --> 00:29:15,120
But as long as…

558
00:29:16,287 --> 00:29:17,622
I can sing on stage,

559
00:29:19,090 --> 00:29:21,059
I didn't care about the noise they made.

560
00:29:24,629 --> 00:29:28,867
So when COVID took away
what I had sacrificed so much for,

561
00:29:29,768 --> 00:29:32,003
I fell into depression.

562
00:29:37,375 --> 00:29:39,144
I waited for over a year…

563
00:29:41,846 --> 00:29:43,114
and now…

564
00:29:44,883 --> 00:29:46,351
I've developed cancer.

565
00:29:50,622 --> 00:29:51,923
And even my singing…

566
00:29:53,858 --> 00:29:55,693
has become awful.

567
00:30:00,165 --> 00:30:02,066
I don't think I can go on.

568
00:30:09,908 --> 00:30:11,309
But you're alive, right?

569
00:30:18,683 --> 00:30:21,352
When I worked at a New York hospital
during COVID,

570
00:30:22,153 --> 00:30:25,657
there was an opera singer
who sang for us like you did.

571
00:30:25,723 --> 00:30:26,791
You know…

572
00:30:27,892 --> 00:30:29,594
that really cheered me up.

573
00:30:32,030 --> 00:30:33,565
I was never able to tell him that,

574
00:30:33,631 --> 00:30:35,133
so I'll say it to you instead.

575
00:30:37,435 --> 00:30:38,536
Thank you.

576
00:30:44,509 --> 00:30:46,778
And I'll tell you this again.

577
00:30:49,914 --> 00:30:50,882
Yes?

578
00:30:52,884 --> 00:30:54,452
Let me operate on you.

579
00:30:57,288 --> 00:30:58,189
What?

580
00:30:59,390 --> 00:31:02,760
I will not fail.

581
00:31:09,467 --> 00:31:10,535
Excuse me.

582
00:31:10,602 --> 00:31:12,770
Dr. Hachisuka, there's big trouble.

583
00:31:12,837 --> 00:31:16,908
Dr. Daimon has begun operating
on Yuika Shiki!

584
00:31:16,975 --> 00:31:17,842
What?

585
00:31:23,548 --> 00:31:24,782
What's going on here?

586
00:31:25,350 --> 00:31:26,784
Why is she operating?

587
00:31:26,851 --> 00:31:28,920
I don't know what's going on either.

588
00:31:28,987 --> 00:31:31,189
You call yourself Director of Surgery?

589
00:31:32,257 --> 00:31:33,491
Dr. Daimon,

590
00:31:33,558 --> 00:31:35,827
we're just waiting
for the chemical surgery

591
00:31:35,894 --> 00:31:37,028
to cure the thyroid cancer.

592
00:31:37,095 --> 00:31:38,363
Surgery isn't necessary.

593
00:31:38,863 --> 00:31:40,431
Aren't you listening?

594
00:31:40,498 --> 00:31:44,102
Dr. Daimon isn't operating
on her thyroid cancer.

595
00:31:45,570 --> 00:31:46,504
You…

596
00:31:46,571 --> 00:31:49,007
This isn't thyroid cancer surgery?

597
00:31:49,073 --> 00:31:54,379
Dr. Daimon is removing a pancoast tumor.

598
00:31:55,313 --> 00:31:56,748
What do you mean?

599
00:31:57,248 --> 00:31:59,417
Besides thyroid cancer,

600
00:31:59,484 --> 00:32:04,722
Yuika Shiki also had cancer
in her pulmonary apex.

601
00:32:08,960 --> 00:32:12,196
Did you notice the pancoast tumor
from the start?

602
00:32:12,931 --> 00:32:13,765
Not at all.

603
00:32:15,133 --> 00:32:18,536
But her elevated CYFRA
in her blood test bothered me.

604
00:32:18,603 --> 00:32:21,139
And there was that other symptom.

605
00:32:21,205 --> 00:32:22,640
Let me see that!

606
00:32:23,374 --> 00:32:25,310
Ms. Shiki, are you all right?

607
00:32:25,376 --> 00:32:26,711
What's more,

608
00:32:26,778 --> 00:32:28,713
even after the chemical surgery,

609
00:32:28,780 --> 00:32:31,049
when Yuika Shiki sang,

610
00:32:31,115 --> 00:32:33,518
there were no clear signs of improvement

611
00:32:33,584 --> 00:32:36,087
such as being able to hold a long note.

612
00:32:42,527 --> 00:32:45,096
Now that you mention it,

613
00:32:45,163 --> 00:32:46,898
her singing then wasn't near…

614
00:32:46,965 --> 00:32:49,334
the 5,000-milliliter lung capacity
she's famous for.

615
00:32:49,400 --> 00:32:51,803
While priority was placed

616
00:32:51,869 --> 00:32:54,906
on treating the thyroid cancer
through chemical surgery,

617
00:32:54,973 --> 00:32:56,641
at the same time,

618
00:32:56,708 --> 00:33:01,145
Dr. Daimon suspected lung disease
and observed the patient.

619
00:33:01,212 --> 00:33:02,981
According to test results,

620
00:33:03,047 --> 00:33:04,649
removal was possible

621
00:33:04,716 --> 00:33:06,617
if surgery was conducted immediately.

622
00:33:07,819 --> 00:33:09,120
Didn't anyone notice?

623
00:33:10,955 --> 00:33:12,323
If I may be so bold,

624
00:33:12,390 --> 00:33:16,227
maybe you were only concerned about
cancer that chemical surgery could cure,

625
00:33:16,294 --> 00:33:19,063
but you weren't concerned
about the patient.

626
00:33:21,099 --> 00:33:22,567
What I'm concerned about is…

627
00:33:23,468 --> 00:33:25,403
medical treatments of the future.

628
00:33:26,471 --> 00:33:30,508
Dr. Daimon is concerned about
the patients she is treating.

629
00:33:32,977 --> 00:33:34,445
- Linear stapler.
- Here.

630
00:33:43,488 --> 00:33:45,957
SURGERY TIME

631
00:34:00,438 --> 00:34:02,974
Right upper lung lobectomy complete.

632
00:34:03,041 --> 00:34:04,909
As fast as ever.

633
00:34:04,976 --> 00:34:06,744
Dr. Daimon! Well done!

634
00:34:06,811 --> 00:34:08,980
- The surgery is a success!
- I'm not done!

635
00:34:09,047 --> 00:34:10,114
What?

636
00:34:10,181 --> 00:34:12,483
We'll remove the thyroid cancer next.

637
00:34:13,351 --> 00:34:14,285
Are you kidding?

638
00:34:14,352 --> 00:34:16,220
It doesn't surprise me anymore.

639
00:34:16,788 --> 00:34:18,489
You've got to be kidding!

640
00:34:18,556 --> 00:34:22,093
Chemical surgery is satisfactorily
curing the thyroid cancer.

641
00:34:22,160 --> 00:34:25,063
One more irradiation
will take care of 99%!

642
00:34:25,129 --> 00:34:27,365
She won't make it
to the stage in time then.

643
00:34:27,432 --> 00:34:30,568
If I do it,
I can cure 100% with this surgery!

644
00:34:30,635 --> 00:34:31,669
Hold on here!

645
00:34:32,670 --> 00:34:34,505
She doesn't want any scars on her neck.

646
00:34:34,572 --> 00:34:35,740
I won't open her neck.

647
00:34:35,807 --> 00:34:37,008
What?

648
00:34:37,075 --> 00:34:39,343
The small incision MHM method.

649
00:34:39,410 --> 00:34:40,511
Small incision MHM method?

650
00:34:40,578 --> 00:34:43,714
- Oh, there is that way!
- What is it?

651
00:34:43,781 --> 00:34:45,716
A two-centimeter incision…

652
00:34:45,783 --> 00:34:48,686
along the clavicle is made
and moved over the location.

653
00:34:49,253 --> 00:34:52,123
Now that chemical surgery
has shrunk the tumor,

654
00:34:52,190 --> 00:34:53,524
it can be removed this way.

655
00:34:53,591 --> 00:34:54,725
- Scalpel.
- Here.

656
00:34:58,696 --> 00:34:59,964
- Bovie.
- Here.

657
00:35:04,102 --> 00:35:05,369
Dr. Daimon…

658
00:35:05,436 --> 00:35:08,039
My neck is on the chopping block.

659
00:35:08,106 --> 00:35:10,408
I won't let anyone's neck get cut.

660
00:35:10,475 --> 00:35:11,309
Okay?

661
00:35:15,246 --> 00:35:17,515
She wasn't worried about my neck.

662
00:35:18,783 --> 00:35:19,784
That makes sense.

663
00:35:19,851 --> 00:35:21,953
It seems like…

664
00:35:22,019 --> 00:35:25,156
she used us, so she could perform surgery.

665
00:35:31,129 --> 00:35:32,597
This means she was…

666
00:35:33,965 --> 00:35:35,700
cured by the Surgery Department.

667
00:35:37,602 --> 00:35:40,505
And the pancoast tumor you missed
was also cured…

668
00:35:41,038 --> 00:35:43,040
by the Surgery Department.

669
00:35:43,574 --> 00:35:44,609
Isn't that right?

670
00:35:47,845 --> 00:35:50,581
Our treatment method
carries a much lower risk.

671
00:35:51,082 --> 00:35:54,952
If her vocal cords are damaged
through surgery,

672
00:35:55,019 --> 00:35:56,587
what will you do for her?

673
00:35:58,222 --> 00:36:00,057
Dr. Daimon!

674
00:36:00,658 --> 00:36:02,493
Say your usual line!

675
00:36:02,560 --> 00:36:03,794
Say it!

676
00:36:03,861 --> 00:36:06,264
The one that starts "I never"! Say it!

677
00:36:06,330 --> 00:36:07,365
Dr. Daimon!

678
00:36:07,899 --> 00:36:09,400
Then I'll say it!

679
00:36:10,735 --> 00:36:11,769
You…

680
00:36:12,537 --> 00:36:13,804
never make mistakes!

681
00:36:13,871 --> 00:36:15,673
- Shut up!
- Sorry!

682
00:36:35,126 --> 00:36:37,595
You did it!

683
00:36:41,933 --> 00:36:42,833
Vitals?

684
00:36:42,900 --> 00:36:46,537
BP 115 over 78, pulse 88, normal sinus.

685
00:36:46,604 --> 00:36:48,372
- We're done.
- Nice work.

686
00:36:48,439 --> 00:36:49,774
- Nice work.
- Nice work.

687
00:36:55,947 --> 00:36:58,482
Now, you can sing
to your heart's content again.

688
00:37:00,718 --> 00:37:02,420
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

689
00:37:10,194 --> 00:37:11,128
Excuse me!

690
00:37:13,664 --> 00:37:16,467
The thyroid cancer surgery
ended in success.

691
00:37:16,534 --> 00:37:17,735
Is that right?

692
00:37:19,237 --> 00:37:21,806
You have prepared
what we agreed on, right?

693
00:37:25,509 --> 00:37:26,611
Don't play dumb.

694
00:37:27,345 --> 00:37:28,546
Your resignation.

695
00:37:29,280 --> 00:37:31,048
You need to keep your promise.

696
00:37:34,585 --> 00:37:36,821
Thank you. As bold as ever.

697
00:37:41,259 --> 00:37:42,293
OFFICIAL APPOINTMENT

698
00:37:42,360 --> 00:37:43,294
TAKASHI EBINA

699
00:37:43,361 --> 00:37:46,063
"You are hereby ordered to transfer
to Noshiro, Akita

700
00:37:46,130 --> 00:37:47,365
Satellite Hospital 49."

701
00:37:48,332 --> 00:37:50,301
What kind of joke is this?

702
00:37:51,569 --> 00:37:53,904
- It's not a joke.
- You scared me! You're here?

703
00:37:53,971 --> 00:37:55,172
Yes, the whole time.

704
00:37:55,840 --> 00:37:58,042
- Takashi Ebina.
- Yes?

705
00:37:58,109 --> 00:37:59,677
Go to Noshiro

706
00:37:59,744 --> 00:38:02,446
and keep up the good work.

707
00:38:02,513 --> 00:38:03,914
Thank you.

708
00:38:03,981 --> 00:38:05,116
I don't understand it.

709
00:38:05,182 --> 00:38:07,752
You don't? Then step over here.

710
00:38:07,818 --> 00:38:09,387
- Sit here.
- Excuse me.

711
00:38:10,187 --> 00:38:15,259
Dr. Hachisuka has something
to say now, so listen to him.

712
00:38:15,326 --> 00:38:17,595
Is that fine?

713
00:38:18,763 --> 00:38:21,999
Yes, Branch Director… I mean…

714
00:38:22,500 --> 00:38:24,168
Acting Hospital Director Hiruma.

715
00:38:26,971 --> 00:38:31,375
Just now, Dr. Hachisuka called me
Acting Hospital Director.

716
00:38:31,442 --> 00:38:33,477
Isn't that wonderful?

717
00:38:33,544 --> 00:38:34,845
You see, for your sake,

718
00:38:34,912 --> 00:38:36,280
Branch Director…

719
00:38:36,947 --> 00:38:39,450
I mean, Acting Hospital Director Hiruma,

720
00:38:39,517 --> 00:38:42,953
I put Surgery's reputation on the line
and recommended surgery.

721
00:38:43,020 --> 00:38:45,423
Yes. I appreciate that very much.

722
00:38:45,489 --> 00:38:46,524
Thank you very much.

723
00:38:46,590 --> 00:38:50,061
But you see, in the future,
there won't be any divisions

724
00:38:50,127 --> 00:38:53,331
like Internal Medicine and Surgery.

725
00:38:53,397 --> 00:38:54,565
Right?

726
00:38:54,632 --> 00:38:58,969
We will be restructuring medicine.

727
00:38:59,036 --> 00:39:01,105
Internal Medicine and Surgery
will be combined

728
00:39:01,172 --> 00:39:03,407
to form the Medical Solutions Division.

729
00:39:04,108 --> 00:39:05,109
Combined?

730
00:39:06,677 --> 00:39:08,045
The medical field…

731
00:39:08,112 --> 00:39:12,216
must evolve its methods and structure
in order to survive.

732
00:39:13,417 --> 00:39:14,251
Dr. Ebina,

733
00:39:14,318 --> 00:39:16,053
I'll sing you a congratulatory song.

734
00:39:17,054 --> 00:39:20,057
Akita's famous song, "Hachimori Hatahata."

735
00:39:20,124 --> 00:39:21,892
And Oga's song, "Buriko."

736
00:39:21,959 --> 00:39:24,028
How about it? Sing with me?

737
00:39:24,095 --> 00:39:25,596
Okay? Go ahead.

738
00:39:26,330 --> 00:39:27,365
Akita…

739
00:39:27,431 --> 00:39:28,332
Akita's famous…

740
00:39:28,399 --> 00:39:31,435
What's wrong with you?
Cheer up, would you?

741
00:39:36,140 --> 00:39:38,209
CANCER SURGERY A SUCCESS,
RETURNS TO REHEARSALS

742
00:39:38,876 --> 00:39:39,977
What's going on?

743
00:39:40,044 --> 00:39:42,246
This isn't what you promised!

744
00:39:43,180 --> 00:39:44,315
Mr. Hachisuka.

745
00:39:44,915 --> 00:39:48,352
This isn't what you promised.

746
00:39:48,419 --> 00:39:51,322
Though it is not a 100% agreeable result,

747
00:39:51,389 --> 00:39:54,692
she was still cured at our hospital.

748
00:39:54,759 --> 00:39:57,695
The effectiveness
of chemical surgery was also--

749
00:39:57,762 --> 00:39:59,096
<i>Who cares about that!</i>

750
00:39:59,630 --> 00:40:01,632
I was going to recommend you…

751
00:40:02,199 --> 00:40:05,536
to head the near-future
medical treatment project.

752
00:40:05,603 --> 00:40:08,038
So this is terribly unfortunate.

753
00:40:08,105 --> 00:40:10,841
I am honored that you considered me.

754
00:40:10,908 --> 00:40:12,810
However, Mr. Okawa,

755
00:40:13,611 --> 00:40:18,382
I don't believe you have the right
to make that decision anymore.

756
00:40:18,449 --> 00:40:20,017
What?

757
00:40:20,084 --> 00:40:21,819
What? Look at this!

758
00:40:28,125 --> 00:40:29,693
ILLICIT AFFAIR REVEALED!

759
00:40:38,169 --> 00:40:39,770
"Only losers have affairs!"

760
00:40:39,837 --> 00:40:41,005
"Quit politics."

761
00:40:41,071 --> 00:40:43,374
"I never want to see this actress again."

762
00:40:43,441 --> 00:40:46,477
In exchange for providing
this information to this tabloid,

763
00:40:46,544 --> 00:40:49,547
they'll publish a special report
on chemical surgery.

764
00:40:49,613 --> 00:40:53,584
Arrange a dinner meeting as soon
as possible with the next person in charge

765
00:40:53,651 --> 00:40:56,287
of the near-future
medical treatment project.

766
00:40:56,887 --> 00:40:58,055
Certainly.

767
00:40:59,790 --> 00:41:01,725
Excuse me.

768
00:41:02,259 --> 00:41:07,798
I would like to thank you for employing
Dr. Daimon and Dr. Jonouchi.

769
00:41:07,865 --> 00:41:09,300
This is a melon.

770
00:41:09,900 --> 00:41:11,669
I wish I could say that,

771
00:41:11,735 --> 00:41:14,738
but Branch Director Hiruma took the melon.

772
00:41:15,539 --> 00:41:19,910
I was told the bill would be handled
by Internal Medicine.

773
00:41:26,116 --> 00:41:27,551
This is exorbitant!

774
00:41:27,618 --> 00:41:28,452
SURGICAL FEES FOR DR. DAIMON

775
00:41:28,519 --> 00:41:31,822
Paying these prices
is ruining the hospital!

776
00:41:32,590 --> 00:41:36,260
She did save Yuika Shiki from cancer…

777
00:41:36,327 --> 00:41:41,232
that Internal Medicine overlooked.

778
00:41:41,298 --> 00:41:44,301
I do not think it is a high price to pay.

779
00:41:49,206 --> 00:41:51,108
Dr. Daimon is…

780
00:41:51,709 --> 00:41:53,611
a superb person.

781
00:41:53,677 --> 00:41:55,546
Thanks to her,

782
00:41:55,613 --> 00:41:58,849
I was able to achieve my goal
of making the case for…

783
00:41:58,916 --> 00:42:00,751
chemical surgery.

784
00:42:02,186 --> 00:42:05,289
Dr. Daimon also achieved her goal.

785
00:42:07,424 --> 00:42:09,527
Her goal…

786
00:42:10,828 --> 00:42:13,230
isn't to perform surgeries,

787
00:42:13,297 --> 00:42:15,432
but to cure patients.

788
00:42:18,669 --> 00:42:21,705
I expect her to continue…

789
00:42:22,339 --> 00:42:24,108
to work for all of us.

790
00:42:24,174 --> 00:42:28,779
And I will continue with my very clear
billing practices.

791
00:42:31,148 --> 00:42:32,216
Here.

792
00:42:40,824 --> 00:42:44,695
<i>I got it! 20 million yen!</i>

793
00:43:21,265 --> 00:43:23,267
SURGERY BRANCH

794
00:43:24,668 --> 00:43:26,537
Thanks for seeing me off, everyone.

795
00:43:26,604 --> 00:43:28,405
I have no regrets.

796
00:43:28,472 --> 00:43:31,141
I got fired for operating on Yuika Shiki,
so I'm satisfied.

797
00:43:33,210 --> 00:43:34,044
Well,

798
00:43:34,111 --> 00:43:36,280
it was Dr. Daimon who operated though.

799
00:43:36,981 --> 00:43:40,184
I'm amazed you can feel satisfied
being treated like this.

800
00:43:40,250 --> 00:43:43,354
Your professionalism
is an example to us all.

801
00:43:43,420 --> 00:43:45,789
Dr. Ebina, you were magnificent!

802
00:43:45,856 --> 00:43:48,092
I'll be back in Tokyo to see the musical.

803
00:43:48,158 --> 00:43:50,260
Let's go drinking then. We'll go Dutch.

804
00:43:50,761 --> 00:43:52,563
Take care, everyone.

805
00:43:53,297 --> 00:43:54,398
Driver, open the trunk.

806
00:43:56,800 --> 00:43:58,702
Thanks for waiting.

807
00:43:58,769 --> 00:44:02,539
Take me to the closest station.

808
00:44:02,606 --> 00:44:06,377
I know the cheapest route,
so go the way I tell you.

809
00:44:09,146 --> 00:44:09,980
See you!

810
00:44:12,316 --> 00:44:14,218
Noisy to the very end.

811
00:44:17,321 --> 00:44:20,357
Dr. Ebina!

812
00:44:22,226 --> 00:44:23,594
He's pretty noisy, too.

813
00:44:24,161 --> 00:44:25,362
He sure is.

814
00:44:26,597 --> 00:44:28,065
<i>She hates groups,</i>

815
00:44:28,132 --> 00:44:29,533
<i>she hates authority,</i>

816
00:44:29,600 --> 00:44:31,135
<i>and she hates restrictions.</i>

817
00:44:32,102 --> 00:44:35,172
<i>Her weapons are</i>
<i>her specialty license and her skill</i>

818
00:44:35,239 --> 00:44:36,807
<i>to work her way up.</i>

819
00:44:37,775 --> 00:44:39,743
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

820
00:44:40,310 --> 00:44:43,213
<i>Also known as… Doctor X.</i>

821
00:44:43,981 --> 00:44:45,215
<i>I'm a freelance nurse.</i>

822
00:44:45,282 --> 00:44:47,351
<i>That is not the job of a surgical nurse.</i>

823
00:44:47,418 --> 00:44:50,554
<i>- You're as unpleasant as ever.</i>
- Is "yes" all you can say, you idiot?

824
00:44:50,621 --> 00:44:52,056
<i>Covering up your mistake?</i>

825
00:44:52,122 --> 00:44:53,357
<i>I was just fired.</i>

826
00:44:53,424 --> 00:44:55,325
<i>Don't ever trust a doctor.</i>

827
00:44:55,392 --> 00:44:56,894
<i>I don't think you see the true risk.</i>

828
00:44:56,960 --> 00:44:58,195
- We're freelancers!
- We're freelancers!

829
00:44:58,262 --> 00:44:59,229
Subtitle translation by: Brian Athey
